# Spanish and English glyph coverage and fallback

## Scope and existing evidence

Connect the existing Spanish/English grapheme inventory, admitted educational
symbols, NFC/NFD accents, Spanish guillemets and punctuation, and custom glyph
fallback to Rust rendering.

The historical accepted theoretical design is preserved in completed P1–P9
records. This record is **open executable integration work**. It must not be
closed merely because a prior design was accepted or a different
implementation was proposed.

## Owner's glyph geometry target (unfinished)

Start from exact reusable geometric primitives, not a collection of random
raster marks. A lowercase **o** is a true circle with center and radius;
a simple single-storey **a** reuses the loop plus a stem. The two-storey
printed **a** is a separate outline, alongside italic and cursive variants.

Allow the user to edit and preview ordered individual pen strokes, choose
each stroke direction, and reverse it explicitly. Add precisely anchored
accents (especially á, é, í, ó, ú), ñ and ü; their placement and stroke
sequence are visible and tunable. The canonical glyph stays unchanged as
width, height, thickness, slant, spacing and regularity are adjusted.

Current saved segment geometry does not establish an analytic-circle glyph
primitive, a built-in two-storey alphabet or automatic joined cursive. These
requirements remain open until visibly rendered and user-editable.

## Executable inventory-only progress — 2026-11-03

